The graph shows two accounts opened with the same deposit at the same interest rate. One pays simple interest and the other compounds annually.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=7.8cm,height=5.8cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=11.4,ymin=0,ymax=6000,xtick={0,2,4,6,8,10},ytick={0,1000,2000,3000,4000,5000},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years},ylabel={Balance (\$)},title={Two accounts at the same rate}]
\addplot[thick,blue,dashed,domain=0:10,samples=2]{2500+200*x};
\addplot[thick,red,domain=0:10,samples=60]{2500*exp(x*ln(1.08))};
\node[blue,right,font=\small] at (axis cs:10,4500) {$B$};
\node[red,right,font=\small] at (axis cs:10,5397) {$A$};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which statement is correct?

Offer P pays $9\%$ p.a. simple interest and Offer Q pays $7.5\%$ p.a. compounding annually, on a deposit of $\$3000$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=7.8cm,height=5.8cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=11.4,ymin=0,ymax=6800,xtick={0,2,4,6,8,10},ytick={0,1000,2000,3000,4000,5000,6000},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years},ylabel={Balance (\$)},title={Offer P and Offer Q on $\$3000$}]
\addplot[thick,blue,dashed,domain=0:10,samples=2]{3000+270*x};
\addplot[thick,red,domain=0:10,samples=60]{3000*exp(x*ln(1.075))};
\node[blue,right,font=\small] at (axis cs:10,5700) {$P$};
\node[red,right,font=\small] at (axis cs:10,6183) {$Q$};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In which year does Offer Q first move ahead of Offer P?
